#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Building-a-Custom-Deb-Package.rst:15
msgid "Building a custom deb package - how-to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Building-a-Custom-Deb-Package.rst:18
msgid ""
"Many Ubuntu users install ROS by using pre-built Debian packages. This "
"article gives a short workflow for building a local custom deb package from "
"a ROS package source directory. After you follow it, you can generate Debian "
"packaging files and build a package for local installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Building-a-Custom-Deb-Package.rst:28
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Building-a-Custom-Deb-Package.rst:30
msgid ""
"Many Ubuntu users install ROS 2 on their system by installing :doc:`deb "
"packages <../../Get-Started/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs>`. This guide "
"gives a short set of instructions to build local, custom deb packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Building-a-Custom-Deb-Package.rst:34
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Building-a-Custom-Deb-Package.rst:36
msgid ""
"To successfully build a custom package, all of the dependencies of the "
"package to be built must be available locally or in rosdep. Additionally, "
"all of the dependencies of the package should be properly declared in the "
"``package.xml`` file of the package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Building-a-Custom-Deb-Package.rst:40
msgid "Install dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Building-a-Custom-Deb-Package.rst:42
msgid "Run the following command to install utilities needed for the build:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Building-a-Custom-Deb-Package.rst:44
msgid ""
"$ sudo apt install python3-bloom python3-rosdep fakeroot debhelper dh-python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Building-a-Custom-Deb-Package.rst:49
msgid "Initialize rosdep"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Building-a-Custom-Deb-Package.rst:51
msgid "Initialize the rosdep database by calling:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Building-a-Custom-Deb-Package.rst:53
msgid ""
"$ sudo rosdep init\n"
"$ rosdep update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Building-a-Custom-Deb-Package.rst:58
msgid ""
"Note that the ``rosdep init`` command may fail if it has already been "
"initialized in the past; this can safely be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Building-a-Custom-Deb-Package.rst:61
msgid "Build the deb from the package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Building-a-Custom-Deb-Package.rst:63
msgid "Run the following commands to build the deb:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Building-a-Custom-Deb-Package.rst:65
msgid ""
"$ cd /path/to/pkg_source  # this should be the directory that contains the "
"package.xml\n"
"$ bloom-generate rosdebian\n"
"$ fakeroot debian/rules binary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Building-a-Custom-Deb-Package.rst:71
msgid ""
"Assuming that all required dependencies are available and that compilation "
"succeeds, the new package will be available in the parent directory of this "
"directory."
msgstr ""
